From: cezanne port
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: describe the visible picture in the pooled buffers' VideoMeta

The stateless decoders set the sink format to the coded size and take the
capture format the driver reports (also the coded size, e.g. 1920x1088) as
the layout of the pooled buffers, while the output caps carry the display
size (1920x1080). The buffers' GstVideoMeta therefore says 1088 rows under
1080-row caps; a downstream videoconvert (videoconvertscale) treats that as
a size change and rescales the coded picture to the caps size instead of
cropping it. The copy path already forces the visible size before copying
for the same reason. Make the shared output-state helper fix the visible
size in the VideoInfo the pool stamps on its buffers; strides, offsets and
the allocation size stay the coded layout.

Found on a MediaTek MT6885 MM21 decoder: every stream whose display size
is not a multiple of the 16x32 tile came out resampled (1080p: 72 dB
against a 1088->1080 bilinear scale of the decoded picture, 31 dB against
the correct crop); streams whose display size equals the coded size were
bit-exact.
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
@@ -754,6 +754,13 @@ gst_v4l2_decoder_set_output_state (GstVideoDecoder * decoder,
 {
   GstVideoCodecState *state;

+  /* The pooled buffers keep the driver's coded layout (strides, offsets,
+   * size), but their VideoMeta must describe the visible picture: with the
+   * coded height under display-size caps a downstream converter rescales
+   * the picture instead of cropping it. */
+  vinfo_drm->vinfo.width = width;
+  vinfo_drm->vinfo.height = height;
+
   state =
       gst_video_decoder_set_output_state (decoder,
       vinfo_drm->vinfo.finfo->format, width, height, reference);
